@page "/terms-and-conditions"
@inherits SitePage

@* The website's terms (legacy's page was placeholder text). Written for how the site works: tours booked and paid online
   in US dollars through Stripe, hostel stays booked through Cloudbeds, guest accounts and enquiries. The cancellation
   and refund terms (sections 5 and 6) are the business's to confirm. *@

<SeoHead Page="Page" PageName="Terms & Conditions" Keywords="terms and conditions, hostel booking, travel terms and conditions, hostel policies"
         MetaDescription="Check out our terms and conditions before booking your stay at Fuse Hostels and Travels. We've outlined our policies to ensure a smooth and enjoyable experience during your travels." />

<LegalPage Id="termsAndConditions" Title="@(Page is null ? "TERMS & CONDITIONS" : PageHeadings.Of(Page, "TERMS & CONDITIONS").Title)">
    <p>Last updated: 25 September 2026</p>
    <p>
        These terms apply when you use this website (fusehostelsandtravel.com), book a tour or a stay with us, or create an account.
        "Fuse", "we", "us" and "our" mean Fuse Hostels and Travel; "you" means the person using the site or making the booking.
        Please read them before booking. By making a booking you confirm that you have read and accept them, on behalf of yourself
        and everyone in your booking.
    </p>

    <h5>1. Who we are</h5>
    <p>
        Fuse Hostels and Travel runs hostels and tours in Vietnam. You can reach us through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>,
        by email at info@fusehostelsandtravel.com, or at 25 Nguyễn Phan Vinh, Cẩm An, Hội An, Quảng Nam, Vietnam.
    </p>

    <h5>2. Using this website</h5>
    <p>
        You may use this site to find out about our hostels, tours and events and to make bookings for yourself and the people
        travelling with you. Please don't misuse it: that includes trying to access other people's accounts or bookings,
        interfering with how the site works, sending spam through our forms, or copying our content, photos or branding for
        commercial use without our permission.
    </p>
    <p>
        We work hard to keep the information on the site (prices, times, availability, descriptions and photos) accurate and up to
        date, but details can change and mistakes can happen. If we find an error in a booking you've made, we'll contact you and
        give you the choice of continuing with the corrected details or a full refund.
    </p>

    <h5>3. Your account</h5>
    <p>
        An account is created with the email address you book with, so that you can see your bookings in My Account. Please keep
        your details accurate and your password to yourself; you're responsible for what's done through your account. If you
        think someone else has used it, tell us straight away. You can download your data or ask us to delete your account at any
        time (see our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>).
    </p>

    <h5>4. Booking tours</h5>
    <p>
        Tours are booked for a particular departure (date and time) and number of guests. Prices are shown and charged in US
        dollars (USD) per guest, and include what the tour's description says they include. Places are limited and are only held
        once your booking is placed, and a booking that isn't paid may be cancelled.
    </p>
    <p>
        Your booking is confirmed when payment is received and we've sent you a confirmation email. Please check it carefully and
        tell us straight away if anything is wrong. The person making the booking must be at least 18 years old and is responsible
        for making sure everyone in the booking knows and follows these terms.
    </p>
    <p>
        Some tours are booked on request: send us an enquiry and we'll confirm availability and price before you pay. An enquiry
        isn't a booking until we've confirmed it and payment has been made.
    </p>

    <h5>5. Payment</h5>
    <p>
        Online payments are taken by card through Stripe, our payment provider; we never see or store your full card details.
        Your bank may charge a fee for payments in US dollars or for converting currency. Where we've agreed that part of a
        booking can be paid later, any balance must be paid before the tour starts; you can pay it from My Account.
    </p>

    <h5>6. Changes and cancellations by you</h5>
    <p>
        If you need to change or cancel a tour, contact us as early as possible with your booking reference. We'll always try to
        move you to another departure if one is available.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you cancel at least 48 hours before the tour's start time, we'll refund what you paid for it. If you cancel less than
        48 hours before the start time, or don't turn up (including missing the pick-up), the tour is non-refundable. Refunds are
        made to the card you paid with and can take 5 to 10 business days to appear, depending on your bank.
    </p>

    <h5>7. Changes and cancellations by us</h5>
    <p>
        Occasionally we may have to change or cancel a tour, for example because of weather, safety concerns, road or sea
        conditions, a minimum number of guests not being reached, or events outside our control. If we cancel, you can choose
        another departure or a full refund of what you paid for that tour. If we have to make a significant change (such as the
        date or a major part of the itinerary), you can accept the change or cancel for a full refund.
    </p>
    <p>
        We're not responsible for costs you've arranged separately, such as flights, transport or other accommodation, if a tour
        is changed or cancelled, so we recommend having travel insurance.
    </p>

    <h5>8. On the tour</h5>
    <p>
        Please be at your pick-up point on time; tours can't wait for late guests. Follow your guide's instructions, especially
        on safety. Some tours involve physical activity, water, heights or road travel: it's up to you to decide whether a tour is
        suitable for your health and fitness, and to tell us about anything we should know before you book. Your guide may refuse
        or end participation for anyone who is intoxicated, puts themselves or others at risk, or behaves unacceptably, without a
        refund. Some tours ask you to sign a waiver before taking part.
    </p>
    <p>
        Tours may be run by our local partners. Where they are, they're chosen by us and follow our standards, and their own
        conditions may also apply on the day.
    </p>

    <h5>9. Staying at our hostels</h5>
    <p>
        Hostel stays are booked through our booking system provided by Cloudbeds, and the prices, payment, deposit and
        cancellation terms for your stay are the ones shown when you book your room. During your stay the house rules at the
        hostel apply, including check-in and check-out times, quiet hours and the rules for shared spaces. You must show a valid
        passport or ID at check-in, as required by Vietnamese law. You're responsible for any damage you cause to the hostel.
    </p>

    <h5>10. Your belongings</h5>
    <p>
        Please use the lockers provided and keep valuables with you. We can't accept responsibility for loss of or damage to
        belongings left unattended at our hostels or on tours, except where it's caused by our negligence.
    </p>

    <h5>11. Travel documents and insurance</h5>
    <p>
        You're responsible for having a valid passport, visa and any other documents you need to travel in Vietnam. We strongly
        recommend travel insurance that covers the activities you book with us, medical costs and cancellation.
    </p>

    <h5>12. Our liability</h5>
    <p>
        We'll provide our services with reasonable care and skill. Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or
        personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that can't be limited by law. Otherwise, our
        liability to you for any booking is limited to the amount you paid for it, and we aren't liable for losses that weren't
        foreseeable, for business losses, or for events outside our reasonable control.
    </p>

    <h5>13. Photos and content</h5>
    <p>
        We sometimes take photos and videos at our hostels, events and tours and may use them on our website and social media.
        If you'd rather not appear, just tell a member of our team. Anything you send us (such as reviews or photos you share with
        us) must be your own and not break anyone else's rights.
    </p>

    <h5>14. Complaints</h5>
    <p>
        If something isn't right, please tell the team or your guide at the time so we can try to fix it. If it can't be sorted
        out then, contact us within 28 days with your booking reference and we'll respond as quickly as we can.
    </p>

    <h5>15. Changes to these terms</h5>
    <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time; the date at the top shows when they last changed. The terms that apply to a
        booking are the ones in place when it was made.
    </p>

    <h5>16. Law</h5>
    <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Vietnam, and any dispute will be handled by the courts of Vietnam. If any part of
        these terms is found to be invalid, the rest still applies.
    </p>
</LegalPage>

@code {
    protected override DefaultIdType PageId => SitePages.TermsAndConditions;
}
